id: BUILD-012
ilities: [modularity]
source: cpm
maturity: 2
action: advisory
title: Vue reactive() assigned to let/var — reassignment breaks proxy
category: build
severity: error
engine: pattern
target:
  extensions: .vue .ts .js
  exclude_paths: test/ tests/ vendor/ node_modules/ .git/ build/ dist/
  content_contains: reactive
patterns:
  - regex: (let|var)\s+\w+\s*=\s*reactive\(
    message: "reactive() assigned to let/var — reassigning the variable replaces the proxy, breaking all reactive bindings"
fix: Use const for reactive objects. Mutate properties instead of reassigning — Object.assign(state, newValues).
